# Trivy vulnerability exceptions — see SECURITY.md for the full rationale.
#
# Advisories that have NO upstream fix are handled generically by
# `--ignore-unfixed` in the CI Trivy step (they cannot be remediated by a
# version bump). This file only lists advisories that DO report a fixed version
# but that we cannot apply directly, each assessed as low risk.
#
# jaraco.context and wheel are not installed as standalone packages — they are
# vendored inside setuptools' `_vendor` tree, so the "fixed" standalone releases
# cannot be applied without an upstream setuptools revendor. Both are build-time
# code paths that the running service never executes.
CVE-2026-23949
CVE-2026-24049
